 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t one objectively “best” company, but for a **long-term rental home**, I’d put **Luxury Property Care (LPC)** on your shortlist. It publishes clear terms: **8–10% of rent collected**, a one-time leasing fee when it places a new tenant, and no management fee while the home is vacant. The company also reports a 4.9/5 Google rating from 230+ reviews; treat that as a company-reported figure and verify it independently.\n\nI’d compare it with **Keyrenter South Florida** and **Real Property Management United**, then ask each for a written, all-in fee schedule and sample management agreement. Compare leasing and renewal fees, maintenance markups, inspection frequency, eviction coordination, cancellation terms, and how quickly they respond to owners. The best fit depends on your home’s location, rent, and whether you want long-term or short-term tenants.",
